    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33762" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păraetăcēnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παραιτακηνή</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a district of Persia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">supra Paraetacenen et Persiden,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 27, 31, § 131</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Curt. 5, 13, 2</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păraetăcae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παραιτάκαι</span>, <i>the
				Parœtacenes</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 8</span></i>; called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păraetăcēni</span></b> , Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παραιτακηνοί</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 26,
				29, § 116</span></i>.</div>
